  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY:\n{自動詞|じどうし} (intransitive)\nPattern: Xが{嵩|かさ}む\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{嵩|かさ}んでいる - has accumulated (resultant state)\n\nWRITING:\nThe kanji {嵩|かさ} is a rare character. This verb is often written in hiragana as かさむ.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {費用|ひよう}が{嵩|かさ}む - expenses mount up\n- {出費|しゅっぴ}が{嵩|かさ}む - spending increases\n- {荷物|にもつ}が{嵩|かさ}む - luggage becomes bulky\n- {年齢|ねんれい}が{嵩|かさ}む - to get older (literary)\n\nUSAGE:\nOften implies a negative connotation, especially when referring to expenses or problems accumulating beyond expectations.",
